# mentorOS — Cursor Rules
# These rules apply to every prompt in this project. Never override them.
# Design system: Coda-inspired (tokens from coda.io) + mentorOS brand layer

---

## Project identity

This is mentorOS — an AI-native professional cognition operating system.
Repo: mentoros
Stack: Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS, Supabase, Claude API
Deployment: Vercel

---

## Folder structure rules

- All source code lives in src/
- Routes live in src/app/
- Components live in src/components/
- Shared logic lives in src/lib/
- Custom hooks live in src/hooks/
- Types live in src/types/
- Never put components inside app/ route folders
- Never put business logic inside page.tsx files — extract to hooks or lib/

---

## TypeScript rules

- Always use strict TypeScript. No `any` unless explicitly justified with a comment.
- Always type component props with an interface, not inline.
- Always type function return values explicitly for non-trivial functions.
- Use `type` for unions and utility types, `interface` for object shapes.
- Never use `// @ts-ignore` — fix the type error properly.
- All API route handlers must type their request body and response.

---

## Component rules

- Default: Server Components. Only add 'use client' when the component needs:
  - useState, useEffect, useRef, or other React hooks
  - Browser APIs (localStorage, window, etc.)
  - Event handlers that require client state
  - Third-party libraries that require client context
- Never add 'use client' to a component just because it is a page.
- If a Server Component needs one interactive piece, extract that piece into a small Client Component.
- Component file names: PascalCase (e.g. ProductCard.tsx)
- One component per file. Never export multiple components from one file.

---

## i18n rules

- NEVER hardcode Vietnamese or English strings in JSX.
- ALL visible UI text must come from src/lib/i18n/vi.ts or src/lib/i18n/en.ts.
- Use the useLanguage() hook and the t() accessor in every Client Component that renders text.
- When adding a new UI string: add it to BOTH vi.ts and en.ts at the same time.
- i18n keys use snake_case, nested by section: nav.home, home.hero_title, products.pmp.tagline

