## Supabase rules

- Never import Supabase client directly in components. Use hooks.
- browser: src/lib/supabase/client.ts
- server:  src/lib/supabase/server.ts
- Never expose SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to the client.
- RLS always enabled. All column names snake_case.
- TypeScript types for DB rows in src/types/database.ts.

---

## API routes rules

- All API routes in src/app/api/
- Always validate request body before processing.
- Never put API keys in client-side code.
- AI provider always called server-side only.
- Rate limiting: add TODO comments, implement later.

---

## AI provider rules

- Primary: Claude (claude-sonnet-4-20250514)
- All AI calls through src/lib/ai/provider.ts
- Never call Anthropic SDK or OpenAI SDK directly from components.
- Always call through /api/ai route from client components.
- System prompts in src/lib/ai/prompts/ — one file per module.

---

## Auth rules

- Supabase Auth with Google OAuth.
- Use useAuth() hook from src/hooks/useAuth.ts.
- Protected routes redirect to /login if no session.
- User data in public.users table synced from auth.users via trigger.

---

## Error handling rules

- Every async function must have try/catch.
- API routes return { data, error } shape.
- Client-side: show user-friendly messages using i18n common.error.
- Never expose raw errors or stack traces to users.

---

