## ============================================================
## MOBILE-FIRST RULES — MANDATORY
## iOS Safari + Android Chrome. Both equal priority.
## ============================================================

## General mobile rules

- Write mobile styles FIRST, then add md: prefix for desktop overrides.
- Never write desktop styles first then try to override for mobile.
- Test mentally at 375px (iPhone SE) before writing any layout.
- Every section, card, and container must look correct at 375px width.

## Touch targets

- Every button, link, and interactive element: min-height h-touch (44px), min-width min-w-touch (44px).
- Use the nav-link class for navbar links to maintain 44px tap area even if visually smaller.
- Never use small close buttons or icon-only buttons under 44px.
- Add padding around small icons to expand tap area if needed.

## Typography on mobile

- Use mobile font sizes as default (no prefix), desktop sizes with md: prefix.
- Pattern for hero headline:
    text-display md:text-md-display font-display font-bold
- Pattern for section heading:
    text-heading md:text-md-heading font-display font-bold
- Pattern for card title:
    text-heading-sm md:text-md-heading-sm font-body font-semibold
- Pattern for body text:
    text-body md:text-md-body font-body
- NEVER use a fixed large size like text-6xl or text-7xl — use the custom scale.

## Spacing on mobile

- Page horizontal padding: px-16 (mobile) px-24 (md:)
- Section vertical gap: py-60 (mobile) md:py-113
- Card padding: p-16 always
- Stack elements vertically on mobile using flex-col, switch to flex-row on md:

## Navbar — hamburger top-right

- Mobile navbar height: h-navbar-mobile (56px)
- Desktop navbar height: md:h-navbar-desktop (64px)
- Fixed position, z-navbar (z-30)
- Include padding-top for iOS safe area: pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)]
- Mobile: show mentorOS wordmark left + hamburger icon button right (44x44 tap area)
- Hamburger opens a RIGHT-SIDE DRAWER (not dropdown, not full screen)
- Drawer width: min(320px, 85vw)
- Drawer has overlay behind it (z-overlay = z-40), drawer itself z-drawer (z-50)
- When drawer opens: add class menu-open to body to lock scroll
- Drawer slides in from right with CSS transition: transform 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)
- Close drawer on: overlay click, close button tap, nav link tap, Escape key
- Desktop: show full nav links inline, hide hamburger

## iOS-specific requirements

- Input font-size MUST be 16px minimum — prevents iOS auto-zoom on focus.
  Always: text-base or style={{ fontSize: '16px' }} on all input/textarea/select.
- Use min-h-screen (100dvh) not 100vh — handles iOS address bar correctly.
- Add -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent to interactive elements (already in globals.css).
- Use -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch on scroll containers.
- Safe area insets for notch (already in globals.css):
    pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)]
    pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)]

## Android-specific requirements

- Test that touch ripple/feedback is disabled (we use CSS transitions instead).
- Ensure font rendering is sharp — -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased is set globally.
- Status bar color controlled via PWA manifest theme_color: #0B1220.

## Grid and layout patterns on mobile

Homepage product cards:
- Mobile: grid-cols-1 (single column, full width)
- md: grid-cols-2 (two columns)

Feature lists / icon+text rows:
- Mobile: flex-col gap-24
- md: flex-row gap-32

Hero section:
- Mobile: text-center, CTA buttons stack vertically (flex-col gap-12)
- md: text-left or text-center (keep center for homepage), CTA buttons in a row

## Scroll behavior

- Use scroll-container class on any overflow-y-auto container for iOS momentum scrolling.
- Use scroll-hidden class to hide scrollbars on horizontal scroll lists.
- Never use overflow: hidden on body unless menu is open.

## Image handling on mobile

- Always use next/image with proper width and height props.
- Use sizes prop: sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw"
- Never use fixed pixel widths on images — always responsive.

## PWA rules

- manifest.json is at /public/manifest.json — already created.
- Icons needed in /public/icons/: 72, 96, 128, 144, 152, 192, 384, 512px PNGs.
- Add to root layout <head>:
    <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0B1220" />
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes" />
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="default" />
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="mentorOS" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icons/icon-192x192.png" />
- Do NOT add a service worker yet — add TODO comment for Phase 5.

## What NOT to do on mobile

- Do NOT use hover-only interactions — always have tap/active states too.
- Do NOT use fixed pixel widths on containers — always use percentages or max-width.
- Do NOT use tiny close buttons under 44px.
- Do NOT put important content behind horizontal scroll without clear affordance.
- Do NOT use backdrop-filter blur heavily — causes performance issues on Android.
- Do NOT animate large elements on mobile — keep animations subtle (fade, small translate).
- Do NOT use 100vh — use 100dvh or min-h-screen from Tailwind (already configured).
